{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 200610, "name": "James Kemp", "username": "jkemp", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/f5a326/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-01-12T23:40:42.369Z", "cooked": "<p>Did a search and found several packages orphaned in the CoreOS of Silverblue.</p>\n<p>libcap-ng-python3<br>\nlibdecor<br>\nliberation-sans-fonts<br>\nliberation-serif-fonts<br>\nlibertas-usb8388-firmware<br>\nlibproxy-duktape<br>\nlibsane-hpaio<br>\nlibsss_sudo<br>\nlibxcrypt-compat</p>\n<p><code>sudo rpm -q --whatrequires</code> I get: no package requires about them.</p>\n<p>How do I get rid of these, being that it’s a read only file system? What effects would it have on the CoreOS? Would they show up in rpm-ostree status if I were able to remove them? Is it even possible? When I try and use DNF in a toolbox these packages are not installed. I guess they aren’t in the container.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-06-22T20:31:37.736Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 111, "reads": 23, "readers_count": 22, "score": 564.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 73598, "topic_slug": "orphaned-packages-in-fedora-silverblue-coreos", "display_username": "James Kemp", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 5, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4238, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/orphaned-packages-in-fedora-silverblue-coreos/73598/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 159216, "name": "Armin Warda", "username": "awarda", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/awarda/{size}/3145_2.png", "created_at": "2023-01-13T06:50:11.849Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jkemp\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"73598\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/f5a326/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> James Kemp:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>libcap-ng-python3<br>\nlibdecor<br>\nliberation-sans-fonts<br>\nliberation-serif-fonts<br>\nlibertas-usb8388-firmware<br>\nlibproxy-duktape<br>\nlibsane-hpaio<br>\nlibsss_sudo<br>\nlibxcrypt-compat</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I checked these packages in my f37 Silverblue installation, and I get a slightly different result:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">awarda@fedora:~$ p=\"libcap-ng-python3 libdecor liberation-sans-fonts liberation-serif-fonts libertas-usb8388-firmware libproxy-duktape libsane-hpaio libsss_sudo libxcrypt-compat\"\n\nawarda@fedora:~$ for n in $p; do echo \"$n: $(rpm -q --whatrequires $n)\"; done | grep \"no package\"\nlibcap-ng-python3: no package requires libcap-ng-python3\nlibdecor: no package requires libdecor\nlibertas-usb8388-firmware: no package requires libertas-usb8388-firmware\nlibproxy-duktape: no package requires libproxy-duktape\nlibsane-hpaio: no package requires libsane-hpaio\nlibxcrypt-compat: no package requires libxcrypt-compat\n\nawarda@fedora:~$ for n in $p; do echo \"$n: $(rpm -q --whatrequires $n)\"; done | grep -v \"no package\"\nliberation-sans-fonts: liberation-fonts-2.1.5-3.fc37.noarch\nliberation-serif-fonts: liberation-fonts-2.1.5-3.fc37.noarch\nlibsss_sudo: sssd-common-2.8.2-1.fc37.x86_64\n</code></pre>\n<p>But IMHO your question is valid.</p>\n<p>Best regards<br>\nArmin.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-03-08T22:39:24.748Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 22, "readers_count": 21, "score": 9.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 73598, "topic_slug": "orphaned-packages-in-fedora-silverblue-coreos", "display_username": "Armin Warda", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 2740, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/orphaned-packages-in-fedora-silverblue-coreos/73598/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 158203, "name": "James Kemp", "username": "jkemp", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/f5a326/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-01-13T08:10:18.644Z", "cooked": "<p>Thanks for responding, Armin</p>\n<p>I see you got a little further. You think the others are standalone packages, excluding the fonts? Why would they get flagged as orphaned?</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-01-13T10:25:38.637Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 21, "readers_count": 20, "score": 4.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 73598, "topic_slug": "orphaned-packages-in-fedora-silverblue-coreos", "display_username": "James Kemp", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 10766, "username": "drongo", "name": "marshall drongo", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/afea85/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4238, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/orphaned-packages-in-fedora-silverblue-coreos/73598/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 175139, "name": "ilikelinux", "username": "ilikelinux", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ilikelinux/{size}/27169_2.png", "created_at": "2023-01-13T11:31:52.479Z", "cooked": "<p>I checked on default workstation (F37),<br>\nthe fonts are from libreoffice-core-7.4.3.2-1.fc37.x86_64<br>\nlibsss_sudo = sssd-common-2.8.2-1.fc37.x86_64</p>\n<p>hope this helps.</p>\n<p>The rest gives no result.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-01-13T11:33:04.510Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 17, "readers_count": 16, "score": 8.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 73598, "topic_slug": "orphaned-packages-in-fedora-silverblue-coreos", "display_username": "ilikelinux", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 53, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Let's have a party (Fedora 44)", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 2081, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/orphaned-packages-in-fedora-silverblue-coreos/73598/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 175142, "name": "James Kemp", "username": "jkemp", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/f5a326/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-01-13T17:48:14.467Z", "cooked": "<p>Thank you, ilikelinux</p>\n<p>I installed LibreOffice as a flatpak. I wonder why they would be in the CoreOS? Let me search and find the location of all these packages. That would explain why they are orphaned.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-01-13T17:48:14.467Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 11, "readers_count": 10, "score": 22.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 73598, "topic_slug": "orphaned-packages-in-fedora-silverblue-coreos", "display_username": "James Kemp", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delet